cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the working paper for the research method and this reference software when reusing the implementation. The portable agent Skill is maintained separately by CrabMods."
type: software
title: "GameSave2Minecraft: Research Reference Implementation"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/crabsatellite/GameSave2Minecraft
url: https://github.com/crabsatellite/GameSave2Minecraft
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Alex Chengyu
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4516-8946
abstract: >-
  Research reference implementation and original reproducible fixture for
  agent-guided migration of game saves into playable Minecraft worlds through
  source adapters, interaction rules and source-bound acceptance. The working
  paper and aggregate case results accompany the implementation; the portable
  agent Skill is maintained in a separate CrabMods repository.
keywords:
  - game preservation
  - cross-game migration
  - Minecraft
  - source-bound evaluation
  - reproducible research
  - reverse engineering
